  "notes": "Measured on N411DX's left side (Haneda 2023-08-27, from above; checked on Boston 2025-06-16 and 2024-03-11). The sweeps' edges are read off by hand and drawn smooth through a few points each; the wing and engine hide their middles, so between x 0.4 and 0.55 low on the body they're estimated (low). The light blue is a gradient on the aircraft, lighter toward the crown; drawn flat. 'TEAM USA' is the scheme's lettering, not a typeface: its stand-in is close in weight and slant only. The fin is Delta's standard (copied from DAL/standard). The right side isn't measured; the photos show it mirrored. The Olympic rings are the IOC's: a renderer may leave them out (no simplified mark proposed)."
